\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Comparison of the three correlation functions $E(\theta )$. The quantum (solid red) and classical (dashed green) correlations only achieve perfect anti-correlation at $\theta =0$. The stronger-than-quantum correlation (dotted blue) is perfect for all angles except $\theta = \pi /2$.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:correlations}{{1}{3}{Comparison of the three correlation functions $E(\theta )$. The quantum (solid red) and classical (dashed green) correlations only achieve perfect anti-correlation at $\theta =0$. The stronger-than-quantum correlation (dotted blue) is perfect for all angles except $\theta = \pi /2$}{figure.1}{}}
